				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														Just adding to Agrivars Idea concerning class improvement, heres magicians<br />
<br />
Well we all know mages are known for their pets, but for some reason I always see magicians grouping when they dont need to, that takes away a lot of experience and playign time, Magicians are made for solo ~Reminder~ just incase you have lost track.<br />
1. Pendign on what race you are if you're in faydwere fight from 1-8 in crushbone and from 8-12 go to the chessboard in bb and SOLO, if your in Antonica fight in EC from 1 - 12.  <br />
2. At 12 you're ready to go to Oasis, it may be hard finding a 12 group at first, but from what ive found its growing more than the idiots who are lvl 18 there and trying to do orc groups still...  ~basically fight in oasis either crocs or orcs from 12 - 15~<br />
3. 15-20 will be your fastest levels if you do this right and don't play hero.  Go to Highpasshold and fight the orcs at the entrance from kith, in a group.  Dont solo this area, very dangerous because the orc spawn rate is quick and you will easily get trained.  Conserve mana, don't blast all away, pending on 2 tanks let the tanks do the work and you  send your pet off and save the mana for the emergency!  There will always be an emergency there.  You will have 20 in a matter of days.  probably for 3-4 hours of work you will have a level.<br />
4. okay if you want to get past 20 and get to 24 for your new spells, go to SK and solo till your head falls off :)  Solo aviaks over at the tree house, if you're a good class you won't be kos so no worrys of mass trains.  Kill rooks and elephants.  Groups are a waste of time afte 20, if you can solo do it, you get 5x more experience, but clarity is a huge helper when soloing so donate for it and sow because sow is a life saver.<br />
<br />
Equipment isn't really important at being a young mage, so save your money for spells, food, etc instead of wasting it on staffs/robes etc...  As long as your pet is adaquate you will do fine no matter if you're twinked like a mother or not, cause if your pet dies, you die.. as simple as that.  Although it can be annoying don't be self concious about asking for pet buffs, most people are sure willing to help and they do make a huge diffrence, even if it is skin like rock.  Any questions about mages and where to get spells etc... don't hesitate to ask...<br />
<br />
~BTW~ Weapons are not important for a mage... don't try and be a tank mage, its ridiculous.  Get low quality int items that are cheap!  Once you get about lvl 30 you will have plenty of money to start upgrading.   <br />
<br />
-Archmage Advisor- Scandaltrik						</td>
